## 🛑 1. The Core Challenge: Monolithic Failure
Traditional web applications (like a standard Node.js/Express server on a tiny Virtual Machine) physically cannot withstand the traffic of 10,000 students logging in to claim free food at the exact same second.

**The Bottlenecks:**
- **CPU Overload:** The single processor freezes trying to calculate 10,000 requests.
- **Database Timeouts:** A standard database instantly rejects connection attempts over its limit (usually 100 max connections), throwing `500 Internal Server Errors` to users.

<br/>

## 🏗️ 2. Our Elegant 4-Pillar Solution

We bypass these failures by utilizing a completely **Decoupled, Stateless, Serverless Micro-architecture**.

| Platform | Architectural Role | Function / Mitigation Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Cloudflare** | Global Edge CDN | Deflects 90% of visual UI traffic from the backend by caching static assets instantly across the globe. |
| **Vercel** | Serverless Compute | Replaces the single server with infinite micro-servers that boot up in milliseconds to perfectly match current traffic, then destroy themselves. |
| **Upstash (Redis & QStash)** | Shock Absorbers | **Redis:** Memory cache providing <5ms read times. <br/> **QStash:** Asynchronous message queue to intercept database writes. |
| **Neon Postgres** | Serverless Storage | Auto-scaling SQL Database with built-in connection poolers. |

