## 🛡️ 4. Heavy-Write Protection Sequence (The QStash Barrier)

> [!WARNING]
> **The Problem Being Solved:** If 1,000 Donors hit `Submit` at the exact same moment, the database connection completely crashes. 
> **The Solution:** We intercept the payloads using QStash, instantly return a success to the frontend, and slowly "drip feed" the heavy transactions into the database securely.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as 🏢 Donor / Student
    participant Vercel as ▲ Vercel (API Layer)
    participant QStash as 📮 QStash (Broker)
    participant Worker as ⚙️ Vercel (Worker)
    participant Neon as 🐘 Neon Database
    participant Pusher as 📡 Pusher (WebSockets)

    User->>Vercel: POST /api/food/create (High Load)
    activate Vercel
    
    note over Vercel: Instantly Serialize Payload
    Vercel->>QStash: publishJSON(payload)
    activate QStash
    QStash-->>Vercel: 200 OK (Accepted by Queue)
    
    Vercel-->>User: 202 Accepted (Response < 50ms)
    deactivate Vercel
    
    note right of QStash: Queue safely absorbs the massive traffic spike.
    
    QStash->>Worker: Webhook: Process Uploads (1 by 1)
    activate Worker
    Worker->>Neon: INSERT ... (Safe Database Write)
    Worker->>Pusher: trigger('food_added')
    Worker-->>QStash: 200 OK (Task Completed)
    deactivate Worker
    deactivate QStash
    
    Pusher-->>User: WebSocket Payload: UI Updates Live!
```

