## ⚡ 5. Serverless Read Acceleration Sequence

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **The Problem Being Solved:** Reading the available food list requires searching through tables. Doing this 10,000 times a second maxes out CPU queries.
> **The Solution:** We intercept the query with Upstash Redis, bypassing the database entirely for 99.9% of user requests.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Hub as 🧑‍🎓 Student Home Page
    participant Function as ▲ Vercel Compute
    participant Redis as 🔥 Upstash Redis
    participant Matrix as 🐘 Neon Postgres

    Hub->>Function: GET /api/food/available
    activate Function
    Function->>Redis: Query: redis.get("availableFood")
    activate Redis
    
    alt Optimal Cache HIT (Sub-10ms)
        Redis-->>Function: JSON String Array
        Function-->>Hub: 200 Fast Response
    else Cache MISS (Rare, only after updates)
        Redis-->>Function: null
        deactivate Redis
        
        note right of Function: Fallback to slow database query
        Function->>Matrix: SELECT * WHERE quantity > 0
        activate Matrix
        Matrix-->>Function: Raw Data Rows
        deactivate Matrix
        
        Function->>Redis: redis.set("availableFood", Data)
        Function-->>Hub: 200 Standard Response
    end
    deactivate Function
```

